# TODO — must-do follow-ups (`./mf`)

- `src/commands/thread/reduced-thread.ts` and `InMemoryTurnStore`
  (`packages/thread-client/src/turns/in-memory-turn-store.ts`) as `./mf`'s
  turn store go when `./mf` gets the shared chat session (one turn store in the package, the
  app's Zustand store as a binding).
  Until then `liveView` compares only reduced status and final text, and the
  "turn not seen from its start" `not_observed` path in `reduced-thread.ts` has
  no test (it is deleted with the file). Removal trigger: the shared chat session lands.

- Card display text, failure copy and interrupt presentation are not in the
  view model yet (`packages/thread-client/src/view/`), so `./mf thread view`
  carries raw card props only. Until they move into the view model, `docs/qa/chat-session.md` says not to compare
  them with the screen. Removal trigger: card display moves into the view model.

- #768 phase 2 (`send` on the run state) owns these known gaps in
  `src/commands/thread/send.ts`, `stream.ts` and `reduced-thread.ts`:
  - `send` reports `timeout` (exit 124) after a Stop that handed its message back
    or cancelled its reply, not `cancelled`. Phase 2 reports the message's own
    disposition: answered, handed back (a `meridian.messages.handed_back` frame
    names it) or still waiting.
  - `ReducedThread` and plain `tail` don't draw queued rows. The package's
    `unheldWriterMessages` and the record's items are ready for when they do;
    `thread view` (the snapshot) already shows them.
  - `RUN_STARTED`'s `executionId`, `reservedForUserTurnIds` and `position` stay
    only because `send`'s interim follow reads them. Phase 2 deletes them, their parser defaults in
    `packages/contracts/src/protocol/run-boundary.ts` and the golden fixture's
    copies together with the interim follow.
  Removal trigger: #768 phase 2 lands.
